  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "4949e92d-0b18-51c0-ad2a-2580f7dfcfa2",
  "slug": "jezebel-chicken-skewers-bake-recipe-11971320",
  "name": "Jezebel Chicken Skewers Bake",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "These Jezebel chicken skewers bake on a bed of Creole-seasoned dirty rice and are glazed with a bold, sweet, and fiery sauce. Made with pineapple preserves, horseradish, mustard, and black pepper, the Southern-style Jezebel sauce brings big flavor to every bite.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C). Place rice in a fine-mesh strainer. Rinse under cold running water until water runs completely clear. Set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Melt 2 tablespoons of the butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add mushrooms and cook, stirring occasionally, until moisture has evaporated and mushrooms are starting to brown, 6 to 8 minutes. Add onion, bell pepper, celery, garlic, thyme, Creole seasoning, and 2 tablespoons butter; cook, stirring often, until vegetables are softened, about 8 minutes. Add 2 tablespoons butter and reserved rice; cook, stirring constantly, until rice starts to toast and turn golden brown, about 2 minutes. Transfer mixture to a 13x9-inch baking dish and stir in stock and scallions; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Stir together apple jelly, pineapple preserves, horseradish, crushed red pepper, dry mustard, and black pepper in a medium bowl until well combined. Transfer half (about 1/2 cup) of apple jelly mixture to a small, microwave-safe bowl; set aside. Add chicken and salt to apple jelly mixture in a bowl; toss to coat. Thread chicken pieces evenly onto skewers, and place on baking dish so that skewers are resting on rim of dish and chicken hovers above rice mixture."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Cover baking dish tightly with aluminum foil."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until broth is mostly absorbed, 50 to 60 minutes. Remove from oven, and increase oven temperature to 500 degrees F (260 degrees C). Add remaining 2 tablespoons of butter to reserved apple jelly mixture and microwave on High until butter is melted, about 1 minute. Discard foil and brush chicken evenly with about half (about 1/4 cup) of the apple jelly mixture."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Bake, uncovered, until all liquid has been absorbed, and chicken is browned, 12 to 14 minutes. Drizzle with remaining apple butter mixture. Divide evenly among 8 bowls; garnish with scallions. Recipe developed by Craig Ruff"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 80,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
